{"parentUuid":"3614fffd-0943-4479-8e83-0b6b921917c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVEd9beifijuM61ij1fy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012ZnBttQrm9JoMBqZcLyfVf","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"r7-blocks","message":"Jarod is dropping Baseplate (the extruded angles look off). Final direction: the ORIGINAL R6 Blocks layout, which is the current live `?brand=blocks` layout with the round-7 header, roles and socials, restyled as a LIGHT theme: a white (or near-white) ground with a pop of a couple of colours. It doesn't have to be cobalt and persimmon. Keep the isometric JT assembly, the dot lattice, the rail and the click. Re-colour the JT so its faces read on white (side faces need real value contrast; no white-on-white).\nQuick round, kept tight: seed from a fresh `pnpm build` (layout unchanged), then make 3 palette-only options, options/L1, L2 and L3, as override CSS limited to colour variables/roles. Make them genuinely different, e.g. (1) cobalt + persimmon on white, (2) a fresh pairing such as ultramarine + coral or green + magenta, (3) something bolder you'd defend. The previous light attempts read as drab, so avoid muddy creams and evenly spread mid-tones: a crisp white ground, ink text, and two saturated colours used deliberately (JT faces, accent words, dot). AA contrast. Shots at 390 and 1440 (plus the intro at the click frame for each); update index.html. Report ≤ 100 words with your pick.","type":"message","recipient":"r7-blocks","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Jarod is dropping Baseplate (the extruded angles …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2841,"cache_read_input_tokens":310745,"output_tokens":1332,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":415},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":